Project: Isotropic Remesher
URL: https://github.com/huxingyi/isotropicremesher
License: MIT (see LICENSE)
Upstream commit: d4674ce63288d7a55a70735181049895aebc3bf7

This is a vendored copy of the isotropic remesher by Jeremy HU. It implements the
five-step isotropic remeshing pipeline (split long edges, collapse short edges, flip
edges, tangential relaxation, project to surface).

Local modifications (all tagged with the comment "BLENDER MODIFICATION"):
  * src/isotropicremesher.h / .cpp
      - Added IsotropicRemesher::setPreserveBoundaries(bool) so callers can choose whether
        open boundary edges are pinned as features.
      - Added an optional progress/cancellation callback argument to
        IsotropicRemesher::remesh(); returning false from the callback stops the loop early
        while leaving the mesh in a valid state.

Files intentionally NOT vendored:
  * test/ (upstream unit test harness and sample .obj models)
  * README.md, .gitignore

Only the headers and translation units required to build the remesher are included, plus
the upstream LICENSE. The build glue lives in CMakeLists.txt. The reusable Blender-facing
wrapper that converts to and from Blender's Mesh lives in
source/blender/geometry/intern/isotropic_remesh.cc.
